Anouk Marchal is a late 20s human female, with red hair and dark brown eyes. She's the fraternal twin of [[Anaïs Marchal|Anaïs]]. Anouk usually wears practical workshop jumpsuits, as anything fancier would likely burn or get stained by one of her experiments. She has a moderately sized raiment of the [[Iridescent Host|Host]].

Anouk is the more technologically-inclined of the twins. Her portion of the [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]] workshop is covered by multimeters, oscilloscopes, and other electrical accoutrement. She tends to be more outgoing than her brother.

In [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/index|Sableclutch]], she maintains a contact who runs a scrapyard — one who prefers to purchase labour directly rather than through any intermediary service, and so regularly offers work to couriers and other hands willing to deal without a middleman.

That contact is [[Copperjaw]], who runs [[Org/Sableclutch Scrap/index|Sableclutch Scrap]].

She builds the rocket hammers she and [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anaïs Marchal|Anaïs]] fight with, and the radios and other devices the Party asks of her.

She and her brother were raised in [[Geography/Fenrith/index|Fenrith]] though born in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]], and speak the language of there between them. The two serve a mistress who, when she cannot be everywhere, sets them to put a finger on the Scale: drawn into a white void over some distant conflict, they tip it toward one side and watch it resolve. She says the same as her brother of their place in the Party's coalition: they are Renge's first, and would answer her if she called them away.
